// CROWN: a function handed on as a value inside its own body recurses
// through whatever it is handed to, where no argument of it can be read for
// a measure. again says it always finishes and hands itself to apply.
// Expect E_EffectMismatch at again.
fn apply(f, x) = f(x)

fn again(x) with !Diverge = apply(again, x + 1)

fn main() = 0
